// ⚠️ `octave absolute` is LOAD-BEARING, not decoration (session 135, measured).
// This book repeats ONE bar of music. In relative octave every repetition starts from
// the previous bar's last pitch, so the music WALKS OFF THE PAGE: perf-slur300 reached
// staff position 10493 by bar 300 and drew 3,146,917 ledger lines = 303 MB of SVG,
// which is where every "seconds per keystroke" number these books ever produced came
// from. Pinned, the same 300 bars are 408 KB and render in 11.8 ms.
octave absolute
// perf fingslur300 (every bar a slur over FOUR fingered notes = the heavy side of the avoid-slur
// #around read: every digit runs CoveringSlurPiece and then a 64-sample walk of the bow, 1200 times.
// Sized like perf-slur300 rather than a 1k book: 1000 bars of scored slurs is minutes per render,
// which is a fixture nobody will run twice. perf-fingbeam1k is the control for the other half of the
// same commit -- fingerings with no scripts and no slurs, the book whose early-out was removed.
part melody

section A {
  melody {
    g'8@finger(1)( g'8@finger(2) g'8@finger(3) g'8@finger(4)) |
    g'8@finger(1)( g'8@finger(2) g'8@finger(3) g'8@finger(4)) |
